<article class="env-theorem" id="02MD">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02MD">Theorem <span data-tag="02MD">6.3.6.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a simplicial set. Then there exists a partially ordered set $(A,\leq )$ and a universally localizing morphism $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(A) \rightarrow S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof of Theorem <a data-tag="02MD" href="/tag/02MD">6.3.6.1</a>.</strong>
       Let $S$ be a simplicial set. Applying Proposition <a data-tag="02MQ" href="/tag/02MQ">6.3.6.14</a>, we can choose a universally localizing morphism $\varphi : \widetilde{S} \rightarrow S$, where $\widetilde{S}$ is a nonsingular simplicial set. Let $A = \operatorname{Sub}_{\operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}}( \widetilde{S} )$ denote the partially ordered set of simplicial subsets of $\widetilde{S}$ which are isomorphic to a standard simplex, so that Corollary <a data-tag="02MP" href="/tag/02MP">6.3.6.13</a> supplies a universally localizing morphism $\lambda _{ \widetilde{S} }: \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(A) \rightarrow \widetilde{S}$. Applying Proposition <a data-tag="02M7" href="/tag/02M7">6.3.5.11</a>, we deduce that the composite morphism 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(A) \xrightarrow { \lambda _{ \widetilde{S} } } \widetilde{S} \xrightarrow { \varphi } S \]
</div>
<p>
       is also universally localizing. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></article>
